# Repository-root ignores.
#
# Scope: things true for *every* agent — OS cruft, editor state, secrets, and
# build output any language might produce. Anything specific to one agent's
# toolchain belongs in that agent's own .gitignore, so the folder stays
# correct if it is ever extracted and used on its own.
#
# Two traps this file deliberately avoids:
#
#   1. `.env.*` — looks reasonable, silently swallows committed templates
#      (.env.sample, .env.template, .env.defaults) and any config that merely
#      starts with `.env.`, such as config/.env.production.yaml. A missing
#      template is invisible: the file just never lands, and the next person
#      to clone cannot run the agent. Only real secret files are listed below.
#
#   2. `tmp/` — with no leading slash this matches a directory named `tmp` at
#      *any* depth, so tests/fixtures/tmp/ disappears. Anchored to the root.
#
# When adding a pattern here, ask whether it could match something an agent
# needs committed. If it could, anchor it or scope it to the agent instead.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------
# Real env files only. Templates (.env.example, .env.sample, .env.template)
# are meant to be committed and are intentionally NOT matched.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- OS ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Editors / IDEs ----------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Build output ------------------------------------------------------
# Unanchored on purpose: these are build artifacts wherever they appear.
# If an agent ever has real source in a folder with one of these names,
# override it in that agent's own .gitignore with a negation.
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# --- Test / coverage artifacts -----------------------------------------
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Language caches ---------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/

# --- Virtualenvs -------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/

# --- Scratch -----------------------------------------------------------
# Root-anchored: a nested tmp/ may be legitimate fixture data.
/tmp/
